      "definition": "urn:stdo:reference-frame:end-to-end-interface-integration:v1 is a composite refinement resolving in REFERENCE_FRAME's urn:stdo:bounded-context:reference-frame-evaluation under the exact selected basis; ASSURANCE supplies its law. It asks whether one outcome remains constructable, understandable and correctly realised across its material interface chain while conserving meaning, authority and cause with sufficient participant context. It relates public boundaries, design, operators, owners and proof to integration, end-to-end and user-acceptance frames, without a fifth testing type, new role or universal gate. Its basis binds one outcome, independent oracle, governing requirements/design, exact checkpoint, contracts and finite cases; design claims bind declared roles/path/dependencies/configuration/capabilities, realised claims actual participants/callables/entry/exit/artifact. Each seam binds domains, pre/postconditions, lifecycle/time, context, mutable subject, refusals and observations. Identities, revisions, units, cardinality, ordering, empty/null/default semantics and validity intervals stay distinct; equal shape/output establishes no equality of meaning, provenance or authority.",
