      "key": "restart_preserves_work_and_unknown_effects",
      "statement": "Discarding context resets neither workspace, applicable valid work nor obligations. Missing contextual/memory/summary traces prove neither undone work, absent effects nor ended effects. Uncertain effect completion remains completion_unknown, or its end remains unestablished beside not_effected, until subject evidence decides. Partial writes are assessed as current material state. Unperformed assessment has no result and is never recorded as performed. No universal reset or full-history replay is required: resuming intake plus work state determines observations and effect reconciliation needed before dependent action. Closed-result handoff retains validity/independence conditions. Safe context disposal requires recording outer-contract-needed step-produced facts before return.",
