          "start_line": 1549
        }
      ],
      "key": "proportional_method_obligations",
      "statement": "Every method constraint identifies removed ambiguity and justifies added reasoning complexity by its contraction of admissible interpretation/realisation space. A bounded symbolic model resolving material alternatives within capacity is proportional even when detailed; divergent implementations, runtime states, tests, reviews and joins are counterfactual evidence of those alternatives, not another numerator. A prior design surface removing no material alternative is disproportionate. Added truth duplication, reconciliation paths or reasoning surface without material ambiguity reduction is disproportionate. Existing obligations should absorb detail where ownership and meaning are preserved. Increased capability may enlarge a resolvable bounded relation but grants no authority, weakens no invariant and waives no acceptance. Owning law may justify a coherent family once, without per-clause rationale fields, receipts or repeated audits.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
