      "key": "resource_declaration_and_measurement",
      "statement": "A limit applies only where declared and states its unit and measured boundary, including counted inputs, actors, processes and repeated reads; its value is stated before the activation. Measure in that unit/boundary where the served obligation needs it. Record outside-boundary consumption as not measured and exclude it from fit claims. Context limit concerns simultaneous active material, including later acquisition: separately report initial bytes, cumulative acquired bytes including repeated reads, and simultaneous bound. Keep measures answering different questions separate. Undeclared, unmeasured or exceeded limits do not establish fit; no universal quota, budget or measurement gate follows.",
