      ],
      "key": "resource_exhaustion_preserves_obligations",
      "statement": "Before exceeding a limit, refine the task, sequence activations, reassign to an actor whose limits fit, or stop with the applicable §3 value naming the limit, such as incomplete when bounded execution ends first. A stop retains unresolved outcome; pressure never permits truncating/omitting material input or obligation. Enlargement re-enters the grant/binding owner. Staying within limits establishes no adequacy; larger limits confer no authority and waive no invariant.",
