      "key": "closed_result_reuse_and_independence",
      "statement": "An unchanged consumer reuses a result only after exact applicability checks. An invalidator withdraws the affected result before reliance even if subject bytes are unchanged, preserving predecessor/successor relation and demonstrably independent surviving results. retain_applicable decides evidence retention on a new basis; change alone proves neither failure nor satisfaction. Domain triggers are instances of the three kinds, never parallel lists. A reused judgment cannot satisfy a separately required independent judgment: the independent assessor acquires its own evidence and supplies its own judgment. Frame revision-coordinate decisions remain REFERENCE_FRAME §10's; touched-result validity is governed here.",
